This file contains the change history for Marinetti and related modules,
plus documentation for the last official release. The list includes but is
not limited to modules which are now LGPLed through the Marinetti Open Source
Project (MOSP).

Not all of these releases were made public, but their changes are listed
for reference.

People who assisted with new information on a bug are listed in brackets.

------------------------
v3.0b5 - 15th March 2012
------------------------

  Init - Made available to Olivier Goguel & Ewen Wannop

- Bumped version number.
- Fixed issues with TCPIPConvertIPToHEX [3509349] (Olivier Goguel)
- Fixed stack imbalance in UDPSYNTAX [3496764] (Olivier Goguel)

  Emulator 1.0 - contributed by Ewen Wannop

- Initial release of Emulator Link Layer to general public

--------------------------
v3.0b4 - 5th February 2008
--------------------------

  Init - Made available to Ewen Wannop

- Bumped version number.
- Improve error handling [1881079]
- Fix pointer addition bug in CopyFromHandle [1885692] (Andrew Roughan)

  CDev

- Bumped version number.

  PPP 1.3d6

- Support for MS-CHAPv1 authentication protocol [498031]
- Handle incoming escape sequences as per RFC [1171684] (Geoff Weiss)

  PPPX 1.3d6

- Handle incoming escape sequences as per RFC [1171684] (Geoff Weiss)

  Uthernet 1.x - contributed by Ewen Wannop and Glen

- Initial release of Uthernet Link Layer to general public

  TCP Snooper - contributed by Kelvin Sherlock

- Initial release of TCP Snooper CDA to general public

-----------------------
v3.0b3 - 17th July 2006 - Kfest
-----------------------

  Init - made available for download from MOSP site

- Added ability to capture TCP trace to disk
- Fixed PROCESSTHIS? Sequence check [226053] (Ewen Wannop)
- Fixed TCPRead memory overrun [426999] (Ewen Wannop)

-----------------------
v3.0b2 - 17th July 2005
-----------------------

  Init

- Fixed stack imbalance in incoming SYN error handler [1084053] (Kelvin Sherlock)
- Fixed stack imbalance in TCPIPStatusUDP [1183332] (Kelvin Sherlock)
- Fixed incorrect usage of MYID in TCPIPLogin [1204455] (Kelvin Sherlock)

  PPPX 1.3d4 - made available for download from MOSP site

- Support for MS-CHAPv1 authentication protocol [498031]

-----------------------
v3.0b1 - 26th July 2003 - Kfest
-----------------------

  Init

- Bumped version number.

  CDev

- Bumped version number.

  MacIP 1.2

- Bumped version number.

  PPP 1.2b1 and PPPX 1.2b1

- Fixed issues with output of debug information

  Casper 1.0.1

- Bumped version number.

  Telnet 1.0.3

- Fixed issue with displaying a message

-----------------------
v3.0d8 - 13th June 2003
-----------------------

First attempt at building the Marinetti installer using scripts developed for MOSP.

  MacIP 1.2d3

- Debug output in format acceptable to Text2Pcap.

  PPP 1.2d9 and PPPX 1.2d9

- Completed the CHAP implementation.
- Debug output in format acceptable to Text2Pcap.

  Telnet 1.0.2

- Fixed problem with closing the connection.

-------------------------
v3.0d6 - 5th October 2002
-------------------------

  Init

- I.QLIB New option in the PtrToPtr routine for checking the from and
to addresses to make sure that any memory moves do not cross out of the
handle. i.e. moves may only be from inside one handle, to the inside of
another. This is handy, because it will _sysFailMgr if any part of Marinetti
tries to move data which crosses a boundary, or is not inside a handle.
- I.PATCH applied to move I.DNR from start of Bank Boundary
- I.DISPATCH Fixed stack imbalance in CallUserTrigger

  PPP 1.2d8 and PPPX 1.2d8

- Support for CHAP Authentication Protocol

  MacIP 1.1a2

- Initial release of MacIP Link Layer to general public

  Casper 1.0f1

- Fixed stack imbalance for TCPIPAcceptTCP call.
- Display server directory location on startup.

  Telnet 1.0.1

- Initial release of version compatible with Marinetti 3.x

---------------------------
v3.0d5 - 16th February 2002
---------------------------

  Init

- ICMP packet sender was using 16 bit even checksum calculation for packets
  which could be either odd or even lengths. This caused an infinite loop
  when trying to send odd length ICMP packets. Fixed. (Andrew - well caught!)

  PPP 1.1a3

- Better way of handling ping of death.

----------------------
v3.0d4 - 6th June 2001
----------------------

  Init

- Fixed stack imbalance in user trigger dispatcher. Also changed callback
  syntax.

----------------------
v3.0d3 - 26th May 2001
----------------------

  Init

- Fixed stack imbalance in ICMPSEND.

  PPP 1.1a2

- New build with some memory corruption checking turned on. We'll see if
  anything pops up.

----------------------
v3.0d2 - 20th May 2001 - Bump the version, people will come...
----------------------

  Init

- Backward compatable link layer modules.
- Bumped version number.

  CDev

- Bumped version number.

-----------------------
v2.1a2 - 27th July 2000 - KFest again? That trick never works!
-----------------------

  Init

- Stack offset problem in ICMP echo reply, so the reply packet was being sent
  as crud. Applied quick fix for KFest, but still problems, as not completely
  patchable without a full build.

--------------------------
v2.1a1 - 12th October 1999 - Just...
--------------------------

  Init

- When in CLOSEWAIT, TCPReadTCP could overrun the requested buffer size. Fixed.

-----------------------
v2.1d1 - 11th July 1999 - It's still living!
-----------------------

  Init

- Initial build with 2.1 version numbers. This is a 2.0.1 and 3.0 hybrid.
- New tool calls _TCPIPGetUserEventTrigger, _TCPIPSetUserEventTrigger,
  _TCPIPGetSysEventTrigger, _TCPIPSetSysEventTrigger.
- New version 2 link layer module interface, with new call LinkConfigFileName.
  Marinetti no longer supports link layer module interface version 1.

  CDev

- Moved buttons around on Setup connection window to make room for longer
  link layer names.
  (Sheppy)

  PPP 1.1a1

- Support for link layer module interface version 2.
- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = PPP.config

  PPP.scripted 1.1a1

- Support for link layer module interface version 2.
- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = PPP.script.cfg

  SLIP 2.1a1

- Support for link layer module interface version 2.
- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = SLIP.config

  Direct Connect 1.1a1

- Support for link layer module interface version 2.
- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = Direct.config

=END=
